# fastp-gpu built-in contamination database
# ============================================================
# Format
# ------
# Lines starting with '#' are comments and are ignored, EXCEPT
# lines of the form:
#
#   # source: NAME
#
# which start a new named source group.  All FASTA entries that
# follow belong to that source until the next '# source:' line.
#
# Source names map directly to the 'sources' array in fastp.json.
# The first two sources (TruSeq, Nextera) reproduce the built-in
# sequences so this file can replace the hardcoded defaults.
#
# To add custom contaminants, append a new '# source:' block at
# the end of this file, or supply a separate file with
#   --contaminant_db /path/to/extra.fa
#
# PhiX 174 calibration spike-in:
#   download the full genome and add it as a new source:
#   wget -q -O - "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=nuccore&id=J02482.1&rettype=fasta&retmode=text" \
#       >> /path/to/fastp-gpu/data/contaminants.fa
# (add "# source: PhiX174" before it)
# ============================================================

